dcmrtstruct2nii
================================================================================
`autoseg_evaluator.core.masks._rasterise_roi_continuous` is ADAPTED FROM
`DcmPatientCoords2Mask.convert` in dcmrtstruct2nii v5
(https://github.com/Sikerdebaard/dcmrtstruct2nii, Zenodo DOI
10.5281/zenodo.4037864). It is not the upstream converter and does not run the
upstream package.

Idea taken from upstream: transform contour vertices to CONTINUOUS (sub-voxel)
image-index coordinates before polygon filling, rather than snapping them to
integer voxel indices first.

Modifications made in this project:
  * Out-of-range slice indices are skipped. Upstream indexes the array with a
    rounded z, so a negative z silently writes into the LAST slice.
  * Contour planarity is checked in continuous index space against a tolerance;
    a non-planar contour aborts the ROI rather than being flattened onto the
    first vertex's slice.
  * An ROI containing any unsupported ContourGeometricType (e.g. the standard
    CLOSEDPLANAR_XOR) returns None rather than an all-background mask, so it is
    reported as a failed conversion instead of a zero-volume structure.
  * The reference image's spacing/origin/direction are restored on the result
    (upstream's engine drops them and repairs this in its facade).
  * The per-vertex coordinate transform is vectorised with NumPy.

